DESCRIPTION >
    Best-effort reproduction of the CollegeVine "Count events with blank
    filter on date-typed JSON field" failure (agents__count.yaml), built
    from telemetry/description only — we never got the real agents__count
    pipe SQL. Hypothesis: once every populated row shares the same type for
    a JSON subcolumn path (a date string), ClickHouse resolves that
    subcolumn to a concrete type instead of a per-row Dynamic value; a row
    that never supplied the key at all then gets that type's zero-value
    default (e.g. a zero date) instead of a true absence, breaking a
    "blank"/"IS NULL"-style filter that used to match it. If wrong once
    Matt's real query is available, replace this file.

SCHEMA >
    `row_id` String `json:$.row_id`,
    `agent_instance_id` Nullable(UInt32) `json:$.agent_instance_id`,
    `action_params_json` JSON `json:$.action_params_json`

ENGINE "MergeTree"
ENGINE_SORTING_KEY "row_id"
